From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GLES: interpolate font texture coordinates at high precision

Text in the GUI at 3840x2160 showed a thin sliver of the neighbouring glyph
at some letters' edges - a one-pixel line at the left of a C, between an E
and a C - and only for some glyphs.

Glyphs sit one texel apart in the font texture, which is linearly filtered,
and RenderCharacter() reaches half a texel past each glyph; in exact
arithmetic the sample at the edge is the centre of the empty gap. But the
GLES font shader is mediump, so the texture coordinate is interpolated at
half precision where the GPU has it (Mali): a coordinate in [0.5, 1) of a
2048-texel texture is only good to half a texel, of a 4096-texel one to a
whole texel - enough to reach the glyph packed next to it. At 4K the font
textures are that wide.

Interpolate the texture coordinate at highp wherever the fragment shader
supports it; the colour stays lowp and the rest mediump.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_fonts.frag | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_fonts.frag
+++ b/system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_fonts.frag
@@ -22,7 +22,11 @@
 
 precision mediump float;
 uniform sampler2D m_samp0;
+#ifdef GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH
+varying highp vec4 m_cord0;
+#else
 varying vec4 m_cord0;
+#endif
 varying lowp vec4 m_colour;
 uniform float m_sdrPeak;
 
